<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-lgiqw — index for the scope=data reaper.

    The baseline changeset deliberately shipped NO expiry index on service_tokens.
    The PRECEDENT for adding one now is the sibling table, inline in that same
    changeset at service-tokens-001-baseline.xml:117-118, where
    idx_session_tokens_expires ships with a comment naming the exact sweep query it
    serves. This index does the same thing for the same shape of query.

    (An earlier version of this comment cited the baseline's line "Active-token
    listing/sweep indexes ... are added by Phase C alongside the queries that need
    them (avoid speculative indexes here)" as a general house rule. That elides the
    qualifier: the sentence reads "for the Phase C CLI" and is scoped to a deferred
    feature, not to sweep indexes at large. The conclusion was right and the citation
    was not, and an ellipsis that drops a scoping clause is how a comment starts
    asserting more than its source does.)

    PARTIAL, on scope='data', because only data rows are ever swept — root, tenant,
    mint and mint-locked are long-lived operator artifacts the reaper never touches.

    On the write cost, since it was argued: the mint path inserts ~313 rows/day
    (measured on the live estate 2026-08-25) — roughly one every five minutes. That
    is not a hot path, and an index maintained at that rate is free. The earlier
    objection ("do not index, it costs the hot mint path") came from reasoning about
    a relative claim without dividing by the day.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="service-tokens-005-1" author="nexus-lgiqw">
        <comment>
            Partial index supporting the scope=data reaper's predicate.
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
-- Data-token reaper (TokenStore.sweepExpiredDataTokens):
--   DELETE FROM nexus.service_tokens
--    WHERE tenant_id = ? AND scope = 'data' AND expires_at &lt; now() - '7 days'::interval
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_service_tokens_data_expires
    ON nexus.service_tokens (expires_at) WHERE scope = 'data';
        </sql>
        <rollback>
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.idx_service_tokens_data_expires;
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
